{"name":"Bloodlust","hex":"#6b1c1a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodlust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A desire for bloodshed and carnage, often aroused in the heat of battle and leading to uncontrolled slaughter and torture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodlust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hematophagy","blocks":[{"text":"Hematophagy is the practice by certain animals of feeding on blood. Since blood is a fluid tissue rich in nutritious proteins and lipids that can be taken without great effort, hematophagy is a preferred form of feeding for many small animals, such as worms and arthropods. Some intestinal nematodes, such as Ancylostomatids, feed on blood extracted from the capillaries of the gut, and about 75 percent of all species of leeches are hematophagous. The spider Evarcha culicivora feeds indirectly on vertebrate blood by specializing on blood-filled female mosquitoes as its preferred prey. Some fish, such as lampreys and candirus; mammals, especially vampire bats; and birds, including the vampire finch, Hood mockingbird, Tristan thrush, and oxpeckers, also practice hematophagy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg/330px-Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematophagy"},{"title":"Bloodlust (Venom song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bloodlust\" is a single released by English speed metal band Venom on August 13, 1982 through Neat Records. It is the bands second single and the follow-up to their debut single \"In League with Satan\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Bloodlust_%28Venom_single%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodlust_(Venom_song)"},{"title":"Bloodlust (Body Count album)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodlust is the sixth album by the American heavy metal band Body Count, released March 31, 2017, by Century Media Records. It is their first recording with new hype man Little Ice, the son of frontman Ice-T."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Bloodlust_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodlust_(Body_Count_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg/500px-Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg/1280px-Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg/500px-Anopheles_stephensi.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Anopheles stephensi mosquito obtaining a blood meal from a human host through its pointed proboscis. Note the droplet of blood being expelled from the engorged  abdomen. This mosquito is a malarial vector with a distribution that ranges from Egypt to China.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnopheles_stephensi.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cimex_lectularius.jpg/500px-Cimex_lectularius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cimex_lectularius.jpg/1280px-Cimex_lectularius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cimex_lectularius.jpg/500px-Cimex_lectularius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bedbug","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACimex_lectularius.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.w